{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:93592",
  "title": "Important: freerdp security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-03 12:05:01"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-04 00:15:15"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "FreeRDP is a free implementation of the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP), released under the Apache license. The xfreerdp client can connect to RDP servers such as Microsoft Windows machines, xrdp, and VirtualBox.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* freerdp: FreeRDP: Denial of Service via uninitialized progressive tile handling (CVE-2026-109242)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap-based buffer overflow during MP3 audio decoding (CVE-2026-110837)\n\n* freerdp: freerdp: Denial of Service via heap out-of-bounds write in NTLM authentication (CVE-2026-111880)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
